# Packing List API — Auth Endpoints
#
# SETUP (do this once before running any request):
#
#   1. Start the server:  go run main.go
#   2. Generate a token:  go run scripts/gen_token.go
#
# Token and host resolve automatically from .env — see requests/README.md
# for how that works. No variables to paste in this file.
#
# GET /me, and /auth/refresh + /auth/logout's rotation/reuse-detection
# behavior (PACK-027), are covered here. Login/callback still need a real
# browser round-trip and aren't — see requests/README.md's "what's
# deliberately not covered" section.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  GET /me
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — returns the authenticated user's profile
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{$dotenv DEV_TOKEN}}

###

### 🔒 401 — no token
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/me


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  POST /auth/refresh — rotation & reuse detection (PACK-027)
#
#  Run top-to-bottom, once. Relies on REST Client's cookie jar
#  (rest-client.rememberCookiesForSubsequentRequests, on by default) to
#  carry each rotated cookie into the next request automatically.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — seeded via the dev refresh token cookie; rotates it
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/auth/refresh
Cookie: refreshToken={{$dotenv DEV_REFRESH_TOKEN}}

###

### ✅ 200 — using the jar's rotated cookie; proves rotation keeps working
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/auth/refresh

###

### 🔒 401 — replaying the original (now-stale) token is reuse, not a refresh
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/auth/refresh
Cookie: refreshToken={{$dotenv DEV_REFRESH_TOKEN}}

###

### 🔒 401 — reuse killed the whole family; even the jar's current cookie now fails
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/auth/refresh


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  POST /auth/logout — server-side revocation (PACK-027)
#
#  Setup: re-run `go run scripts/gen_token.go` first — the section above
#  killed the dev family, so this needs a fresh one. No separate cleanup
#  section: gen_token.go deletes the dev user's prior refresh_tokens rows
#  on every run.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — logout revokes the family server-side
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/auth/logout
Cookie: refreshToken={{$dotenv DEV_REFRESH_TOKEN}}

###

### 🔒 401 — refresh after logout fails: revoked server-side, not just cookie-cleared
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/auth/refresh
Cookie: refreshToken={{$dotenv DEV_REFRESH_TOKEN}}
